#
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Project-Id-Version: PLUMED-TUTORIALS\n"
"Language: ja\n"
"MIME-Version: 1.0\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"
"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n"

#: input.md:1
msgid "Input files preparation"
msgstr "入力ファイルの準備"

#: input.md:3
msgid ""
"In the zip file available in the [GitHub "
"repository](https://github.com/compsb-unimi/VMetaD-tutorial) you will find "
"all the initial files needed to run this tutorial."
msgstr ""
"[GitHub リポジトリ](https://github.com/compsb-unimi/VMetaD-tutorial) の ZIP "
"に、実行に必要な初期ファイルがすべてあります。"

#: input.md:5
msgid "Preliminary molecular dynamics run"
msgstr "事前の Molecular Dynamics"

#: input.md:6
msgid ""
"As a first step for the VMetaD run, we have to choose the atoms which will "
"constitute the reference frame on which we will calculate the position of "
"the ligand with respect to the protein. To be sure in choosing residues that"
" remain stable (i.e. do not belong to a moving loop), we run a 100 ns-long "
"plain molecular dynamics (MD) simulation at 300 K (that is the temperature "
"at which we will run and analyze all the simulations in this tutorial). This"
" run took 2 h on 4 CPUs of a M1 Max MacBook Pro)."
msgstr ""
"まず、タンパク質に対する Ligand の位置を計算する参照座標系の原子を選びます。動く Loop などを避け、安定な残基を選ぶため、300 K "
"で100 ns の通常 MD を実行します。この Tutorial の全シミュレーション・解析は同じ温度です。M1 Max MacBook Pro の4"
" CPU で2時間かかりました。"

#: input.md:8
msgid ""
"After the simulation, we calculate the per-residue root mean square "
"fluctuations (RMSF), which highlights the more dynamic residues."
msgstr "実行後、残基ごとの Root Mean Square Fluctuations (RMSF) を求め、動きの大きい残基を確認します。"

#: input.md:16
msgid ""
"We can see that almost all the C-terminal domain (residues 71-162) does not "
"show large fluctuations, and only few residues are above the (arbitrary) "
"RMSF threshold of 0.15 nm. We thus consider to define the reference frame "
"considering all the residues 71-162 but the five ones with RMSF > 0.15 nm "
"(residues 135, 136, 137, 140, and 141)."
msgstr ""
"C-terminal Domain（71〜162）のほぼ全体で揺らぎは小さく、任意に定めた RMSF 0.15 nm "
"の閾値を超える残基はわずかです。したがって71〜162のうち、RMSF > 0.15 nm "
"の5残基（135、136、137、140、141）を除いて参照座標系を定めます。"

#: input.md:18
msgid "PDB file for reference frame refitting"
msgstr "参照座標系の再 Fit 用 PDB"

#: input.md:19
msgid ""
"To be sure to keep the structure stable during the simulation, we will "
"define the reference frame of VMetaD on the residues selected for the fit. "
"To have a reference structure to be used in PLUMED (see the next section for"
" the input file), we convert the initial structure to the PDB format using "
"`gmx editconf` (to ensure consistency with the numbering) and keeping only "
"the C-alphas:"
msgstr ""
"シミュレーション中も構造を安定に保つため、Fit に選んだ残基で VMetaD の参照座標系を定めます。PLUMED "
"用の参照構造として、番号の整合性を保つため `gmx editconf` で初期構造を PDB に変換し、C-alpha "
"のみを残します。入力は次の節で説明します。"

#: input.md:24
msgid ""
"Remember to add the correct values to the b-factor columns (and/or removing "
"unwanted atoms for the fitting procedure) telling PLUMED which are the atoms"
" we want to use for the fitting procedure (see the `ref_ca.pdb` file in the "
"folder for reference)."
msgstr ""
"B-factor 列に適切な値を入れるか、不要な原子を除き、Fit に使う原子を PLUMED に指定してください（付属の `ref_ca.pdb` "
"を参照）。"

#: input.md:26
msgid "Choice of the restraining potential size"
msgstr "Restraint Potential の大きさの選択"

#: input.md:28
msgid ""
"We now need to choose the size of the restraint potential. In the [original "
"paper](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jpclett.9b01183) we showed that the "
"reliability of the estimates is not affected by the size of the potential. "
"However, we have to keep in mind that we need a part of the box where the "
"ligand can stay far away from the protein in order to represent the unbound "
"state in a satisfactory way. An important point here is that the sphere "
"constraint __must__ be inside the box, otherwise the entropic correction "
"will not accurately account for the loss of configurational space. To "
"visually inspect how large the potential is, and to get a feel for the "
"possible movements of the ligand, we can visualize both the system and the "
"restraint with VMD (downloadable "
"[here](https://www.ks.uiuc.edu/Research/vmd/))."
msgstr ""
"次に Restraint Potential "
"の大きさを選びます。[原著](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jpclett.9b01183) "
"では、推定の信頼性がその大きさに依存しないことを示しました。ただし非結合状態を十分に表すには、Ligand がタンパク質から離れられる領域が Box "
"内に必要です。球形拘束は __必ず__ Box 内に収めてください。外に出ると Configuration 空間の減少を Entropy "
"補正で正しく扱えません。大きさと Ligand "
"の可動範囲を確認するには、VMD（[こちら](https://www.ks.uiuc.edu/Research/vmd/)）で系と Restraint "
"を表示できます。"

#: input.md:30
msgid ""
"We can open VMD and load the `starting.gro` structure file in the GitHub "
"folder. After the structure is loaded and the visualization has been set up "
"at your taste, you can open the Tk console and write"
msgstr ""
"VMD を開き、GitHub の `starting.gro` を読み込みます。好みの表示に設定し、Tk Console で次を入力します。"

#: input.md:34
msgid "which draws the cubic box in which the system is inserted."
msgstr "系を含む立方体 Box が描かれます。"

#: input.md:36
msgid ""
"Now we can generate the atom selection we defined after checking the RMSF:"
msgstr "次に、RMSF の確認後に決めた原子選択を作ります。"

#: input.md:40
msgid "The console should answer"
msgstr "Console は次のように返すはずです。"

#: input.md:44
msgid ""
"Where `XX` is a number. The selection for the reference frame has been "
"defined and named `$sel`. Now we can compute the position of the center of "
"mass of this set of atoms:"
msgstr ""
"`XX` は数値です。参照座標系用の選択が `$sel` として定義されました。次に、この原子群の Center of Mass を計算します。"

#: input.md:48
msgid ""
"The console should answer with the position of the center of mass (in "
"Ångstrom)"
msgstr "Center of Mass の位置が Ångstrom 単位で返されます。"

#: input.md:52
msgid ""
"Knowing this information, we can draw the sphere with a radius of (for "
"example) 2 nm (20 Å) with the following command"
msgstr "この情報から、例えば半径2 nm (20 Å) の球を次で描けます。"

#: input.md:56
msgid ""
"Receiving a number as an answer from the console. Such number is the ID of "
"the 3D object we just draw. The drawn sphere is opaque, not allowing us to "
"see inside it; to make it transparent, we need to specify that we want a "
"transparent material"
msgstr ""
"Console が返す数値は、描いた3D Object の ID です。球は不透明で内部が見えないため、透明な Material を指定します。"

#: input.md:60
msgid ""
"We can see that the sphere contains the entire domain, but it is probably "
"too small to represent the unbound state in a precise way. Let's delete the "
"sphere using the ID of the 3D object (let's say that it is `14`), and plot a"
" new sphere of radius 2.8 nm"
msgstr ""
"球は Domain 全体を含みますが、非結合状態を正確に表すには小さすぎるようです。3D Object の ID（例えば "
"`14`）で球を削除し、半径2.8 nm の球を描き直します。"

#: input.md:66
msgid "You can see the expected result below"
msgstr "期待される結果を以下に示します。"

#: input.md:73
msgid "The PLUMED input file"
msgstr "PLUMED 入力ファイル"

#: input.md:74
msgid ""
"_(You can read the following line-by-line description keeping an eye on the "
"`plumed.dat` file in the GitHub folder as a reference)_"
msgstr "_以下の各行の説明は、GitHub の `plumed.dat` を参照しながら読めます。_"

#: input.md:76
msgid "Reference frame setup"
msgstr "参照座標系の設定"

#: input.md:77
msgid ""
"We start with the `WHOLEMOLECULES` instruction, to be sure that lysozyme "
"(`ENTITY0`) will not be broken by the periodic boundary condition, as well "
"as the benzene molecule (`ENTITY1`):"
msgstr ""
"まず `WHOLEMOLECULES` で、Periodic Boundary Conditions により Lysozyme（`ENTITY0`）と "
"Benzene（`ENTITY1`）が分断されないようにします。"

#: input.md:81
msgid ""
"Now that we are sure of the integrity of the structures in PLUMED, we "
"perform the rototranslational fit of the system to make sure that the "
"protein will be in the fixed reference frame position:"
msgstr "構造がつながったら、系を回転・並進して Fit し、タンパク質を固定した参照座標系に置きます。"

#: input.md:89
msgid ""
"We then start with the groups definition. We previously prepared a GROMACS "
"index file (`index.ndx`) with all the groups named as intended. As an "
"alternative, you can also define such groups with atom ids."
msgstr ""
"次に Group を定義します。事前に必要な名前の Group を含む GROMACS Index `index.ndx` を用意しました。Atom "
"ID で直接定義することもできます。"

#: input.md:100
msgid "We have three groups:"
msgstr "3つの Group があります。"

#: input.md:101
msgid ""
"`prot_noh`, which contains all the non-hydrogen atoms of the protein (for "
"our multi-eGO potential is equivalent to all the protein, but in all-atom "
"representation it makes a difference);"
msgstr "`prot_noh`：タンパク質の非水素原子。multi-eGO では全タンパク質と等価ですが、All-atom では違いがあります。"

#: input.md:102
msgid ""
"`sph`, which contains the atoms that define the reference frame (the C-alpha"
" of the selected residues -see above-);"
msgstr "`sph`：参照座標系を定める原子（上記で選んだ残基の C-alpha）。"

#: input.md:103
msgid "`lig`, which contains the atoms of the ligand."
msgstr "`lig`：Ligand の原子。"

#: input.md:105
msgid ""
"After the definition of the groups, to avoid that the passage in a periodic "
"boundary conditions causes a \"jump\" of the ligand with respect to the "
"protein, we add a `WRAPAROUND` instruction:"
msgstr "Group 定義後、PBC を越えた Ligand がタンパク質に対して Jump しないよう `WRAPAROUND` を加えます。"

#: input.md:118
msgid "Ending the fitting part of the PLUMED input."
msgstr "これで入力の Fit 部分が完了します。"

#: input.md:120
msgid "Spherical coordinates definition"
msgstr "球座標の定義"

#: input.md:121
msgid ""
"We now compute the position of the center of mass of the atoms defining the "
"reference frame ($(x,y,z)=(0,0,0)$ in our CV space), and the center of mass "
"of the ligand:"
msgstr ""
"参照座標系の原子群の Center of Mass（CV 空間で $(x,y,z)=(0,0,0)$）と Ligand の Center of Mass"
" を計算します。"

#: input.md:140
msgid ""
"From the position, we can obtain the cartesian coordinates of the ligand in "
"this reference frame"
msgstr "これらの位置から、この座標系での Ligand の Cartesian Coordinates を求めます。"

#: input.md:163
msgid ""
"and via the usual transformation, obtain the final spherical coordinates "
"$(\\rho,\\theta,\\varphi)$"
msgstr "通常の変換で、最終的な球座標 $(\\rho,\\theta,\\varphi)$ を得ます。"

#: input.md:190
msgid "which will be our CVs."
msgstr "これらを CV とします。"

#: input.md:192
msgid "Restraining"
msgstr "Restraint"

#: input.md:193
msgid ""
"We now have to impose the spherical restraint. We put a `UPPER_WALLS` which "
"impedes the ligand to go farther than 2.8 nm:"
msgstr "球形 Restraint を加えます。`UPPER_WALLS` で Ligand が2.8 nm より遠くに行かないようにします。"

#: input.md:222
msgid ""
"the $k$ value is 10,000 kJ/mol/nm^2, which means that if the ligand is out "
"by 0.1 nm he will feel a potential of 100 kJ/mol."
msgstr "$k$ は10,000 kJ/mol/nm^2 なので、0.1 nm 外に出ると100 kJ/mol の Potential を受けます。"

#: input.md:224
msgid ""
"One effect that we should take into account is the possibility that the "
"ligand, in advanced phases of the simulation, will try to unfold the "
"protein, being the place occupied by it the volume portion with less "
"history-dependent potential deposited. To limit this phenomenon we will put "
"in place a RMSD restraining that will be removed during the reweighting "
"procedure. To compute the RMSD we will use the same atoms included in the "
"`ref_ca.pdb` file instruction"
msgstr ""
"後半では、履歴依存 Potential が最も少ないタンパク質の占める体積へ Ligand が入り、Unfolding "
"を起こす可能性があります。抑えるため RMSD Restraint を加え、Reweighting で除きます。RMSD は `ref_ca.pdb` "
"の原子で計算します。"

#: input.md:257
msgid "Reweighting CVs"
msgstr "Reweighting 用 CV"

#: input.md:258
msgid ""
"As anticipated in the theory part, to compute binding free energy "
"differences we will need to reweight our free energy landscape on new apt "
"CVs which will allow us in discriminating efficiently the bound and unbound "
"states. Like in the original work, here we will use again the distance from "
"the origin of the reference frame $\\rho$ and the number of contacts between"
" the protein and the ligand. This will guarantee that if the guest can be "
"considered not in contact with the host (and thus defining the unbound "
"state), even if $\\rho$ is large."
msgstr ""
"理論編のとおり、結合自由エネルギー差には、結合・非結合状態を効率よく区別する CV への Reweighting "
"が必要です。原著と同じく、参照座標系の原点からの距離 $\\rho$ と、タンパク質・Ligand 間の Contact "
"数を使います。これにより、$\\rho$ が大きい場合にも Guest が Host と Contact していないか確認し、非結合状態を定義できます。"

#: input.md:260
msgid "The total number of contact $c$ is defined with a switching function"
msgstr "全 Contact 数 $c$ は Switching Function で定義します。"

#: input.md:267
msgid ""
"which runs on all the (heavy) atoms of the protein and all the atoms of the "
"ligand. This is implemented with `COOORDINATION`:"
msgstr "タンパク質の全 Heavy Atom と Ligand の全原子について計算します。`COOORDINATION` で実装します。"

#: input.md:301
msgid "where we set a $r_0$ parameter at 0.45 nm."
msgstr "$r_0$ は0.45 nm とします。"

#: input.md:303
msgid "Volume-based Metadynamics"
msgstr "Volume-based Metadynamics"

#: input.md:304
msgid "We now set up the VMetaD:"
msgstr "次に VMetaD を設定します。"

#: input.md:351
msgid ""
"The most exotic option used is `CALC_RCT`, which allows the calculation on "
"the fly of the [Tiwary-Parrinello "
"estimator](https://doi.org/10.1021/jp504920s) that we will use for "
"reweighting."
msgstr ""
"特徴的なのは `CALC_RCT` で、Reweighting に使う [Tiwary-Parrinello "
"Estimator](https://doi.org/10.1021/jp504920s) を On-the-fly に計算できます。"

#: input.md:353
msgid "Printing"
msgstr "出力"

#: input.md:354
msgid ""
"We finally print all the relevant files that we will use for post-processing"
" and analysis."
msgstr "最後に、後処理・解析に必要な全ファイルを出力します。"

#: input.md:410
msgid ""
"We will have all the VMetaD quantities in `metad_data.dat`, the restraints "
"data in `{rmsd,sphere}_restaint.dat`, the $(x,y,z)$ and "
"$(\\rho,\\theta,\\varphi)$ coordinates in `xyz_coord.dat` and "
"`rtp_coord.dat`, respectively, and the reweighting CVs in `coord_rho.dat`."
msgstr ""
"VMetaD の量は `metad_data.dat`、Restraint は "
"`{rmsd,sphere}_restaint.dat`、$(x,y,z)$ と $(\\rho,\\theta,\\varphi)$ はそれぞれ "
"`xyz_coord.dat`、`rtp_coord.dat`、Reweighting CV は `coord_rho.dat` に出力します。"

#: input.md:412
msgid ""
"___PLEASE NOTE___: all the printing frequencies are synchronized with the "
"VMetaD `PACE` (every 10 print we deposit 1 gaussian), and it should be "
"synchronized also with trajectory printing (I personally suggest the same "
"frequency used for gaussian deposition). This allows us to restart safely in"
" case of issues and re-run or re-analyze with new CVs the run, if needed."
msgstr ""
"___注意___：出力頻度は VMetaD の `PACE` と同期しています（10回の出力ごとに Gaussian 1個を追加）。Trajectory"
" の出力とも同期させてください。Gaussian 追加と同じ頻度を推奨します。問題時の安全な再開や、別の CV による再実行・再解析が可能になります。"

#: input.md:414
msgid "Last advices before launching the simulation"
msgstr "実行前の最後の助言"

#: input.md:415
msgid ""
"One issue that can be observed when launching when running VMetaD is the "
"sudden interruption of the simulation with a cryptic error. Please check the"
" position of the ligand: in most cases, the system reached "
"$(\\rho,\\theta,\\varphi)=(0,0,0)$, where the derivatives of the potential "
"cannot be defined, and thus PLUMED sends an error. Despite being annoying, "
"this is perfectly normal, and does not invalidate the run. Please restart it"
" from the previous checkpoint (save a checkpoint often!)."
msgstr ""
"VMetaD が突然、わかりにくいエラーで止まることがあります。Ligand の位置を確認してください。多くは系が "
"$(\\rho,\\theta,\\varphi)=(0,0,0)$ に達し、Potential "
"の微分が定義できなくなるためです。不便ですが正常なことで、計算全体が無効になるわけではありません。前の Checkpoint "
"から再開してください。Checkpoint は頻繁に保存しましょう。"

#: input.md:417
msgid ""
"Another consideration regarding the singularity of the reference frame is "
"its position with respect to the actual binding site. In close proximity of "
"it (let's say less than 2 sigmas in $\\rho$) even an extremely small "
"movement in any direction makes the ligand move of several sigmas in "
"$\\theta$ and $\\varphi$, with the possibility of underestimation of the "
"bias. This could imply the need of longer simulation times to fill up the "
"basin. To limit this effect, we suggest to verify if the origin of the "
"reference frame is farther that 2-3 sigmas in $\\rho$ from the binding site "
"(the perfect situation would be setting the origin in a point occupied by "
"the host, at 4-5 Å from the binding site)."
msgstr ""
"座標系の特異点と実際の結合部位の位置関係にも注意します。原点の近く（$\\rho$ の2 Sigma 未満程度）では、わずかな移動でも "
"$\\theta$ と $\\varphi$ が数 Sigma 変化し、Bias を過小評価する可能性があります。そのため Basin "
"を埋める時間が長くなる場合があります。原点が結合部位から $\\rho$ の2〜3 Sigma "
"より離れているか確認してください。理想は、結合部位から4〜5 Å 離れた Host 内の点です。"

#: input.md:419
msgid "Launch!"
msgstr "実行！"

#: input.md:420
msgid ""
"You can now run the VMetaD tutorial. We advice you to run it for (at least) "
"500 ns. In this example, we run it for 1 µs."
msgstr "VMetaD を実行できます。少なくとも500 ns を推奨します。この例は1 µs です。"

#: input.md:422
msgid "[Back to VMetad home](NAVIGATION.md)"
msgstr "[VMetad のホームに戻る](NAVIGATION.md)"
